# L §8.4 R-load (tally 2.1.7, R5, issue #144, the builder's SR-B1, pick P40): a leg's unit fault only the run meets
# (a leg of unit any whose amount is a bare 0, between places of two units a binding over the accounts gives) is
# RUN-DOMAIN at the values that read the instance, in load's words; no LOAD-* code prints at run, and the run goes on.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
kind anys: event certain
  leg cash: any
input d1: date
input z: num
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place kasa: accounts EUR lives 2026-01-01..

move nil[p in accounts on d1, q in accounts on d1 where p != q]: anys
  on d1
  leg cash from p to q amount z

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)

ask f: flows(nil, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d1 = 2026-03-01
  z = 0
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[kasa] = 0 EUR at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
b: refused: RUN-DOMAIN the amount of leg cash of nil[kasa, konto] (0) is in no unit of a place
  cut 2026-01-01
f: refused: RUN-DOMAIN the amount of leg cash of nil[kasa, konto] (0) is in no unit of a place
  cut 2026-01-01
